course: dictionary
lesson: 7237
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Piano is a musical instrument, and it is also a word a music teacher uses to mean play softly. The words around piano tell you which meaning to use.
explain: «She sat down at the piano and played a tune.» Here piano is the big instrument, because you sit at it and play it. «Play the start of the tune piano, then get louder.» Here piano is an instruction about how loud to play.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If the word could be counted, like two pianos, it is the instrument. If it tells you how to play, it means softly.
fact: A piano is a big musical instrument with black and white keys.
fact: When you press a key, a small hammer hits a string inside the piano, and the string makes a sound.
fact: A piano usually has 88 keys, and longer strings make lower notes.
fact: In music, piano means play softly. Its opposite is forte, which means play loudly.
fact: The plural of piano is pianos. Some -o words add -es (potatoes, tomatoes), and others add -s (pianos, photos, zoos).
exercise: «The grand piano filled the big hall with music.» What is a piano in this sentence? | A type of musical note | A soft, quiet tune | *A big musical instrument with black and white keys | A small hammer that hits the keys
exercise: Mrs Hale writes «piano» on the board above a tune. What does piano mean? | Stop playing and sit down | Play as fast as you can | Play loudly | *Play softly
exercise: What is the plural of piano, meaning more than one? | pianoe | pianies | pianoes | *pianos
test: «The pianos in the music room were out of tune.» What does pianos mean here? | Quiet, soft tunes | A kind of potato | *More than one piano | The music teacher's name
test: The teacher says, «Play this part piano.» What should you do? | Play it loudly | Sing the notes backwards | Put the lid down and stop | *Play it softly
exam: What does piano mean in «Please play the start of the tune piano, then get louder.»? | Very fast | *Softly | Loudly | A big instrument with black and white keys
